{"entries":[[2484,"ôter","verb",4,"/o.te/","",[2025,"Fr-%C3%B4ter.ogg.mp3"],[["to take away, remove","",[],[],[]],["to take off, remove (clothes, etc.)","",[],[],[["Le guichetier de garde vient d'entrer dans mon cachot, il a ôté sa casquette, m'a salué, s'est excusé de me déranger et m'a demandé, en adoucissant de son mieux sa rude voix, ce que je désirais à déjeuner.","The duty hatchman just came into my cell, took off his cap, gave me a salute, said he was sorry for bothering me and asked me, whispering as best he could with his rough voice, what I wanted for lunch.",""]]],["to remove, cut (text etc.); to take away (in arithmetic)","",[],[],[]],["to take (something) away from someone; to deprive","",[],[],[["La guerre […] / Nous ôta tout","The war […] / deprived us of everything",""]]],["to move oneself, get out of the way","",["pronominal"],[],[]]],{"infinitive":"ôter","auxiliary":"avoir","present_participle":"ôtant","past_participle":"ôté","present":["ôte","ôtes","ôte","ôtons","ôtez","ôtent"],"imperfect":["ôtais","ôtais","ôtait","ôtions","ôtiez","ôtaient"],"future":["ôterai","ôteras","ôtera","ôterons","ôterez","ôteront"],"conditional":["ôterais","ôterais","ôterait","ôterions","ôteriez","ôteraient"],"subjunctive":["ôte","ôtes","ôte","ôtions","ôtiez","ôtent"]},["ôter la vie","ôter une épine du pied","ôter les mots de la bouche"],""],[3757,"otage","noun",4,"/ɔ.taʒ/","",[3153,"Fr-otage.ogg.mp3"],[["hostage","",[],[],[["Prendre (quelqu'un) en otage.","To take (someone) as a hostage.",""]]]],{"plural":"otages"},["prendre en otage"],""],[16461,"otarie","noun",2,"/ɔ.ta.ʁi/","f",[13192,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-J%C3%A9r%C3%A9my-G%C3%BCnther-Heinz_J%C3%A4hnick-otarie.wav.mp3"],[["sea lion","",[],[],[]]],{"plural":"otaries"},[],["La marée n'échoue plus sur ces sables l'otarie moustachue, aux oreilles enroulées, aux mâchelières pointues, se traînant sur ses pattes sans ongles."]],[17199,"otite","noun",2,"/ɔ.tit/","f",[13776,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-DenisdeShawi-otite.wav.mp3"],[["otitis (inflammation of the ear)","",[],[],[]]],{"plural":"otites"},[],["Le traitement médical de l'otite chronique connaît l'une ou l'autre amélioration, notamment avec les perméabilisants des tissus."]],[18476,"Ottoman","noun",2,"/ɔ.tɔ.mɑ̃/","m","",[["Ottoman (member of the Ottoman dynasty)","",[],["Osman","Osmanide","Osmanli"],[]],["Ottoman (citizen of the Ottoman Empire)","",[],["Osman","Osmanide","Osmanli"],[]]],{"plural":"Ottomans","feminine":"Ottomane"},["turc ottoman"],""],[18491,"ottoman","adjective",2,"/ɔ.tɔ.mɑ̃/","",[14809,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-WikiLucas00-ottoman.wav.mp3"],[["Ottoman","",[],["osmanide","osmanli"],[]]],{"masculine":"ottoman","feminine":"ottomane","masculine_plural":"ottomans","feminine_plural":"ottomanes"},["turc ottoman"],["Très bientôt, sous le règne de Mehmed II, Constantinople allait tomber aux mains de la dynastie ottomane.","L'infanterie ottomane monte bravement à l'assaut des positions ennemies sur les collines d'Eptchéli, puis de Koyounli.","Le monde musulman put alors s'enorgueillir de quatre États célèbres : L'Égypte de Mamelouks, la Turquie ottomane, la Perse séfévide et l'Inde moghole."]],[18492,"ottoman","noun",2,"/ɔ.tɔ.mɑ̃/","m",[14809,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-WikiLucas00-ottoman.wav.mp3"],[["ottoman","",["uncountable"],[],[["La dame avait une robe / En ottoman violine","",""]]]],{},["turc ottoman"],""],[28479,"ottomane","noun",1,"/ɔ.tɔ.man/","f",[23053,"LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Lyoko%C3%AF-ottomane.wav.mp3"],[["ottoman","",[],[],[]]],{"plural":"ottomanes"},[],["Sur le premier plan, à gauche de l'acteur, une ottomane placée dans un petit réduit demi-circulaire et orné de tapisseries.","Après avoir achevé ce grand ouvrage, je courus avec mes vers chez ma bien-aimée. Je la trouvai seule dans un négligé charmant, assise sur une ottomane."]],[32852,"otospongiose","noun",1,"","f","",[["otospongiosis","",[],[],[]]],{"plural":"otospongioses"},[],""],[34632,"oto-rhino-laryngologique","adjective",1,"/ɔ.to.ʁi.no.la.ʁɛ̃.ɡɔ.lɔ.ʒik/","",[27912,"LL-Q150_%28fra